Design a Clock Data Recovery (CDR) module that extracts a clean clock signal from incoming data. This module utilizes a phase-locked loop architecture to track the phase of the clock relative to the data input. It includes a phase accumulator that adjusts based on a control signal derived from the phase difference between the current and previous clock states. A voltage-controlled oscillator (VCO) is simulated to generate a varying output clock signal, which is then divided down by a configurable value to produce the final clock output. The module effectively synchronizes the output clock with the input data, making it suitable for applications in high-speed data communication.
