description:
Create a clock gating circuit that outputs a clock signal (ENCLK) when both the enable (EN) and test enable (TE) signals are high, in conjunction with the input clock (CLK). This design effectively allows the clock signal to be selectively passed through based on the state of the EN and TE inputs, serving to reduce power consumption in digital circuits by disabling the clock to certain parts of the circuit when not needed.
module top_module(
  input CLK, EN, TE,
  output ENCLK
);

